From: elkir0 <elkir0@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 13/16] spi: s3c64xx: allow for the auto chip-select gap in the
 DMA timeout

With S3C64XX_SPI_QUIRK_CS_AUTO the controller idles NSC_CNT clocks
around every frame, so a long byte-wide transfer runs well below
cur_speed. The SS333 BOOT image (10748 bytes at 100 kHz on SPI4 of
Exynos5433) moved at about 67 kbit/s and timed out after 8056 bytes
against a 0.93 s budget. The vendor 3.10 kernel multiplied the
computed time by 10; do the same for auto chip-select ports.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/spi/spi-s3c64xx.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/spi/spi-s3c64xx.c b/drivers/spi/spi-s3c64xx.c
index bd75c9c96..9ec34db9e 100644
--- a/drivers/spi/spi-s3c64xx.c
+++ b/drivers/spi/spi-s3c64xx.c
@@ -577,6 +577,13 @@ static int s3c64xx_wait_for_dma(struct s3c64xx_spi_driver_data *sdd,
 
 	/* millisecs to xfer 'len' bytes @ 'cur_speed' */
 	ms = xfer->len * 8 * 1000 / sdd->cur_speed;
+	/*
+	 * Auto chip select idles NSC_CNT clocks around every frame, so a long
+	 * byte-wide transfer runs well below cur_speed (about 2/3 of it at
+	 * 100 kHz on Exynos5433); keep the vendor kernel's tolerance.
+	 */
+	if (sdd->port_conf->quirks & S3C64XX_SPI_QUIRK_CS_AUTO)
+		ms *= 10;
 	ms += 30;               /* some tolerance */
 	ms = max(ms, 100);      /* minimum timeout */
 
